static const unsigned char app_apps_README_md[] =
    "# cwick apps\n\nEach app is a self-contained H5 bundle und"
    "er `apps/<id>/`; `manifest.json`\nlists what the built-in"
    " app market shows. The server embeds this tree into the\n"
    "binary (see `tools/embed_web.c`) and serves it at `/apps"
    "/...` on the same\norigin as the OpenAI API, so an app ne"
    "eds no build step, no package manager and\nno CORS config"
    "uration.\n\nLayout:\n\n```\napps/\n  manifest.json          # "
    "the market catalog\n  tictactoe/             # \344\271\235\345\256\253\346\240\274\344"
    "\272\225\345\255\227\346\243\213\n    app.json             # app metadata (kept n"
    "ext to the code)\n    index.html           # entry\n    ap"
    "p.css\n    app.js\n  kart/                  # 3D \346\263\241\346\263\241\345\215\241"
    "\344\270\201\350\275\246\n    app.json\n    index.html\n    app.css\n    app.j"
    "s\n  imagegen/              # H5 image + video studio (tw"
    "o steps)\n    app.json\n    index.html\n    app.css\n    app"
    ".js\n```\n\nThe decision apps (tictactoe, kart) ask the mod"
    "el through `POST /v1/systemone`;\n`imagegen` calls the im"
    "age endpoints `/v1/images/edits` and\n`/v1/images/generat"
    "ions` in step one, then the async `/v1/videos` job in st"
    "ep\ntwo (see the two-step section below). The chat tab ke"
    "eps using\n`/v1/chat/completions`. Every request an app m"
    "akes is same-origin \342\200\224\nthere is no configurable externa"
    "l endpoint. The resident model is discovered\nfrom `GET /"
    "v1/models` and re-discovered after a server-side switch,"
    " so the\ndecision adapter always follows the checkpoint t"
    "hat is actually loaded.\n\nTo add an app: create `apps/<id"
    ">/`, add its entry to `manifest.json`, then run\n`make` ("
    "which builds and runs the C generator `tools/embed_web`)"
    " and restart\n`cwick serve --web`.\n\n## Where an app keeps"
    " its data\n\n**Not** in `localStorage` alone. The server o"
    "wns the databases in `~/.cwick/apps/`\n(`--store DIR`, or"
    " `$CWICK_STORE`): **one file per app**, `<id>.db`, plus "
    "`auth.db`\nfor the server's own API keys. A `--store` pat"
    "h that exists as a file or ends in\n`.db`/`.sqlite` still"
    " means one shared database \342\200\224 the old layout \342\200\224 and ev"
    "ery\napp's rows then live in that one file behind their `"
    "app_id`.\n\nRun from a checkout, `--store ./apps` puts eac"
    "h app's database right next to its\ncode (`apps/tictactoe"
    ".db`, `apps/kart.db`). That is deliberate and safe:\n`too"
    "ls/embed_web.c` skips every database suffix when it walk"
    "s `apps/`, so a\nrunning server's files are never compile"
    "d into the binary, and `.gitignore`\nkeeps them out of a "
    "commit.\n\nThree generic collections per app, all behind t"
    "he same login as the model:\n\n```\nGET    /v1/store       "
    "                   layout, per-app row counts, file size"
    "\nGET    /v1/store?app=<id>                 that app's ow"
    "n database\nGET    /v1/apps/<id>/state                eve"
    "ry key            -> {\"items\":[...]}\nGET    /v1/apps/<id"
    ">/state?key=K          one value            -> {\"value\":"
    "<json>}\nPUT    /v1/apps/<id>/state                {\"key\""
    ":K,\"value\":V} or {\"values\":{...}}\nDELETE /v1/apps/<id>/s"
    "tate?key=K\nGET    /v1/apps/<id>/events?game_id=G&limit=N"
    "\nPOST   /v1/apps/<id>/events               {\"game_id\",\"s"
    "eq\",\"kind\",\"payload\"}\nGET    /v1/apps/<id>/games?limit=N"
    "        newest first\nPUT    /v1/apps/<id>/games         "
    "       {\"game_id\",\"started_at\",\"ended_at\",\"outcome\",\"mov"
    "es\"}\nDELETE /v1/apps/<id>/games?game_id=G      the game "
    "and its events\n```\n\nEvery value and payload must be JSON"
    "; it is stored as the exact text that\narrived and handed"
    " back verbatim, so an app never has to match a schema th"
    "e\nserver invented. `<id>` is `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}` \342\200\224 c"
    "hecked before it reaches\nsqlite \342\200\224 and limits are 1 MiB"
    " per value / payload and 5000 rows per read.\n\nWhy a serv"
    "er-side store rather than `localStorage`:\n\n- \"clear site"
    " data\", a private window or a second browser profile wou"
    "ld erase a\n  match history the model produced;\n- the pho"
    "ne that scanned the QR is a different browser and must s"
    "ee the same\n  scoreboard and history;\n- an app's history"
    " is worth keeping after the tab is gone.\n\n`apps/tictacto"
    "e` uses all three collections: `state` for the scoreboar"
    "d, `games`\nfor one row per match (`started_at`, `ended_a"
    "t`, `outcome`, `moves`) and\n`events` for one row per mov"
    "e (`kind` = `human`/`ai`, payload = board snapshot,\nprom"
    "pt with the per-cell tactical facts, the model's full pr"
    "obability\ndistribution as `probs`, raw model answer, par"
    "sed move, latency, usage). The\nright-hand column's **\345\216\206"
    "\345\217\262\345\233\236\346\224\276** tab reads them back and replays a finished g"
    "ame\nstep by step.\n\n`apps/kart` uses the same three: `gam"
    "es` for one row per run (`moves` = obstacles\nthe model p"
    "laced), `events` for `kind` = `spawn`/`hit`/`lap`/`end` "
    "(payload = the\nobstacle type, the position on the strip,"
    " the kart's speed, the model's latency,\nits raw answer, "
    "plus the variation `seed`, pressure `focus` and decision"
    "\n`entropy`) and `state` for the best score and a lifetim"
    "e tally. Every spawn is a\nmodel decision, so the replay "
    "shows what the model actually said for each\nobstacle rat"
    "her than a number from a generator.\n\n## Which apps decid"
    "e, and through which endpoint\n\nBoth hosted apps ask the "
    "model to choose, and both call `POST /v1/systemone`.\nThe"
    " chat tab is a different consumer: it uses `/v1/chat/com"
    "pletions`, because a\nconversation is generated text, not"
    " a choice among options.\n\n- **tic-tac-toe** \342\200\224 the huma"
    "n plays X first. Each machine move is a `choice`\n  over "
    "the empty cells, and the question is explicitly *which c"
    "ell gives O the\n  greatest probability of winning*. The "
    "state carries the board and one line of\n  tactical facts"
    " per empty cell (immediate win, forced block, winning re"
    "plies,\n  open lines). Those are facts, not a ranked list"
    ": the old wording \342\200\224 \"win, else\n  block, else centre, e"
    "lse corner\" \342\200\224 was a local rule dressed up as a questio"
    "n\n  and was removed. `fallbackMove()` remains, but only "
    "for a failed request.\n- **kart** \342\200\224 a 12-way `choice` o"
    "f obstacle kind and lane, asked in real time\n  while the"
    " kart is moving. The question now asks for *maximum diff"
    "iculty*; the\n  previous \"leave room for the player to re"
    "act\" was the opposite of the goal.\n\nWhat stays local is "
    "what a letter cannot express: the kart's obstacle distan"
    "ce\nis derived from speed (and tightens with the lap, abo"
    "ve a reaction floor). The\nmodel decides *what*, the app "
    "computes *where* \342\200\224 and an app never substitutes a\nloca"
    "lly generated obstacle for a model decision.\n\nAny app th"
    "at caches a model id must handle a switch on the server "
    "side: a 400\nwhose text says the model is no longer serve"
    "d drops the cached id, rediscovers\nthe resident model an"
    "d retries once. `GET /v1/systemone` answers which family"
    ",\nprompt grammar and letter set are live, so a client ca"
    "n check rather than\ninfer.\n\n## The win-probability reado"
    "ut in `apps/tictactoe`\n\n`cellFacts()` computes, for each"
    " empty cell and each mark, whether the move\nwins immedia"
    "tely, whether it blocks the opponent's immediate win, ho"
    "w many\nwinning replies remain, and how many lines are st"
    "ill open. It never ranks or\npicks a cell \342\200\224 it is the s"
    "ame information a human counts, rendered into the\nstate "
    "and into each option's description. The endpoint's softm"
    "ax over the\noption letters is the model's distribution o"
    "ver \"which cell wins most\"; its\nargmax is the move.\n\nThe"
    " right-hand column draws one bar per empty cell, highlig"
    "hts the cell\nactually played, and shows the human's own "
    "tactical facts on their move, so\nboth sides of the game "
    "have a decision trail. The bars are a readout of one\npre"
    "fill, **not** a Monte-Carlo win rate, and the heading sa"
    "ys so: calling them\na simulated win percentage would be "
    "a claim the endpoint cannot make.\n\n## The model decides "
    "the obstacles in `apps/kart`\n\n`pumpAgent()` runs once pe"
    "r frame while racing and keeps at most one request in\nfl"
    "ight and a two-deep queue of decisions, because a kart c"
    "overs ~13 m in the\ntime a 320B model takes to answer \342\200\224"
    " so the model is asked about a stretch of\ntrack 45\342\200\22395 "
    "m ahead rather than about the next frame.\n\nThe question "
    "is a 12-way `choice` at `/v1/systemone`: four obstacle k"
    "inds times\nthree lanes, one letter each. The model never"
    " writes a lane offset or a\ndistance \342\200\224 numbers it would"
    " have to generate token by token, and then be\nrepaired w"
    "hen it wrote prose around them. The distance is derived "
    "locally from\nthe kart's speed, which also keeps the road"
    " readable: the player sees where the\nthing will be, not "
    "just what kind it is. The state is one line of English f"
    "acts: lap, speed, hits, obstacles ahead,\nspawned so far,"
    " difficulty level, which side of the strip is up, a vari"
    "ation\nseed and a pressure point. Every byte is prefill o"
    "n every obstacle, which is\nwhy the option labels are sho"
    "rt English and the Chinese names stay in the\nsidebar.\n\n*"
    "*Real-time random decisions.** The readout is determinis"
    "tic for a fixed\nprompt, and a fixed A..L order would put"
    " the model's letter bias on the same\nobstacle every time"
    ". Each request therefore Fisher-Yates shuffles the twelv"
    "e\noptions (`criteria` is an ordered object on the server"
    ", so member order becomes\nthe letters), draws a fresh va"
    "riation seed and one of six pressure points, and\nasks fo"
    "r the hardest obstacle it can choose. The variation live"
    "s in the\n*question*, never on the road: the seed, pressu"
    "re point and the normalised\nentropy of the resulting dis"
    "tribution are shown in the sidebar and written to\nthe sq"
    "lite `agent`/`spawn` events, so it is auditable rather t"
    "han hidden.\n\n**There is no local generator behind it.** "
    "This is the requirement, not an\naccident: an empty queue"
    " means an empty road, the HUD says `\346\250\241\345\236\213\347\246\273\347\272\277 \302\267 \346\232\202\344"
    "\270\215\346\224\276\350\267\257\351\232\234`,\nand the sidebar's `\345\267\262\346\224\276\350\267\257\351\232\234` can never"
    " exceed the model's successful decisions.\nThe alternativ"
    "e \342\200\224 silently inventing obstacles when the model is slo"
    "w \342\200\224 makes\nthe statistics a lie and hides a broken inte"
    "gration behind a playable game.\n\nThree traps this app ha"
    "s already hit, all worth remembering:\n\n- the model id mu"
    "st be the one the server advertises (`GET /v1/models`), "
    "never a\n  literal \342\200\224 an invented name is a 400 and the "
    "model is never asked at all;\n- `ensureModel()` returns t"
    "he discovery promise from `resolveModel()`, which\n  cach"
    "es the in-flight `GET /v1/models` so several obstacles s"
    "pawned in one\n  frame share a single lookup. An empty an"
    "swer must not be cached, or one cold\n  start would leave"
    " the game without obstacles for the whole run. Failures "
    "like\n  that are invisible on screen \342\200\224 the road is just"
    " empty for a moment \342\200\224 so the\n  model state is exposed "
    "under `?debug`;\n- a model id cached before a server-side"
    " switch is refused on *every* call\n  (\"model `x` is not "
    "served by this endpoint\"). A 400 with that text now drop"
    "s\n  the id, rediscovers the resident model and retries o"
    "nce;\n- one decision is one prefill, and the endpoint tak"
    "es a generation slot: on this\n  single-slot server an ob"
    "stacle decision queues behind a chat turn. That is why\n "
    " the queue is only two deep and why an empty queue is sh"
    "own as an empty road\n  rather than papered over.\n\n## The"
    " 3D renderer in `apps/kart`\n\nNo WebGL, no library: the k"
    "art is a small triangle rasteriser on a 2D canvas.\nEach "
    "frame it pushes ~700 triangles into one buffer (track qu"
    "ads, curbs, centre\nand edge lines, quarter-lap gates, ob"
    "stacle boxes, the kart), sorts them\nfar-to-near and fill"
    "s them. Three details carry the whole thing:\n\n- **camera"
    " space is forward-positive.** `toCam()` dots a point wit"
    "h (right, up,\n  forward) from the eye, so z > 0 means in"
    " front; the projection divides by z and\n  a Sutherland\342\200"
    "\223Hodgman clip against `z >= NEAR` trims the polygons tha"
    "t straddle\n  the camera. An earlier version used the Ope"
    "nGL convention (forward = \342\210\222z) in the\n  view matrix whi"
    "le the clip assumed +z, which culled the entire world;\n-"
    " **normals are normalised before shading.** The cross pr"
    "oduct of a quad's edges\n  has length = its area (a road "
    "segment is 8.8 m by 1.7 m, so |n| \342\211\210 15); using\n  that "
    "directly as a brightness factor saturates every large qu"
    "ad to white,\n  which is exactly how one build turned the"
    " strip into a white slab;\n- **the camera's up vector is "
    "the surface normal**, so the horizon rolls with the\n  st"
    "rip instead of staying level with the world. That is wha"
    "t makes the flip\n  readable rather than a floating camer"
    "a over a twisted ribbon;\n- **road texture must be indexe"
    "d by world position, not by segment index.** The\n  bandi"
    "ng and centre dashes were picked with `i & 1` over the w"
    "indow the camera\n  draws; because that window moves with"
    " the kart, the pattern moved with it and\n  the road look"
    "ed painted on the lens \342\200\224 93 km/h and nothing on the su"
    "rface said\n  so. Snapping the segments to a world grid ("
    "`first = floor(u / du)`) makes the\n  stripes stream past"
    ". A chase cam also needs a spring: with the eye an exact"
    "\n  function of the kart's position, acceleration shows n"
    "othing; a few metres of\n  lag, a 2 cm bob and a focal ki"
    "ck with speed are what \"driving\" looks like.\n\nThe track "
    "is a parametric M\303\266bius strip, `S(u, v) = C(u) + A(u)\302\267v"
    "` with\n`A(u) = cos(u/2)\302\267radial + sin(u/2)\302\267up`, so afte"
    "r one lap the across direction is\nreversed \342\200\224 one side,"
    " one surface, and the gates built in that frame arrive\nu"
    "pside down half a lap later.\n\nThe strip is drawn in two "
    "zones: the near ~1.3 rad at full detail (banding,\nkerbs,"
    " dashes, painted start/twist bands) and the rest out to "
    "4.4 rad as one\ncoarse quad per 0.08 rad plus a bright ri"
    "m. Without the far zone a M\303\266bius track\nis indistinguish"
    "able from a banked ring \342\200\224 you only ever see the ten me"
    "tres under\nthe kart. The rim is what carries the shape: "
    "a M\303\266bius strip is recognised by its\nsingle continuous e"
    "dge.\n\nA chase camera sits *inside* the twist, which is e"
    "xactly why the app also draws a\nsmall inset: the whole l"
    "oop from outside the ring, with up-facing faces teal and"
    "\ndown-facing faces violet so the half-twist shows as a c"
    "olour flip, plus the\nkart's dot. Its projection is writt"
    "en separately from the main camera on\npurpose \342\200\224 the ma"
    "in camera is a per-frame function of the kart and must n"
    "ot be\ndisturbed by a 140-pixel diagram. `?debug` exposes"
    " `window.__kart` (`G`, `AGENT`,\n`tris()`, `frameAt`) so "
    "a headless run can tell \"zero triangles\" from \"triangles"
    "\nbehind the camera\".\n\n## Sharing on the LAN\n\n`cwick serv"
    "e --lan` binds all interfaces (no auth/TLS; trusted Wi-F"
    "i only) and\nprints e.g. `LAN share: http://192.168.71.84"
    ":8001/apps/tictactoe/`. **Every app\nhere carries a \345\210\206\344\272"
    "\253 / \344\272\214\347\273\264\347\240\201 button** \342\200\224 it calls `GET /v1/share?app=<"
    "id>` and\nrenders the answer through `GET /v1/share/qr?te"
    "xt=<url>`; scanning the PNG opens\nthat app standalone on"
    " a phone. Two things are worth knowing:\n\n- **the `?app=`"
    " is not optional for a new app.** The server's default i"
    "s\n  `tictactoe`, so an app that forgets it will happily "
    "hand out a QR for somebody\n  else's page. The id is char"
    "set-checked before it reaches `printf`.\n- **`shareable:f"
    "alse` is a real answer**, returned with a `warning` when"
    " the\n  listener is loopback-only or has no LAN IPv4. The"
    " sheet shows the reason and\n  the `--lan` hint instead o"
    "f a code that would not resolve.\n\n\nWith `--lan`, cwick f"
    "orces single-user login, so an unauthenticated phone is\n"
    "redirected to `/login?next=/apps/<id>/` and returns to t"
    "he app after the\npassword \342\200\224 which is why every share n"
    "ote says the first open needs it. The apps\nare responsiv"
    "e (tested at 390 px) and do not need the main console sh"
    "ell when\nopened from that URL \342\200\224 the kart opens straigh"
    "t into its race because that is all\nit does.\n\n## The two"
    "-step workflow in `apps/imagegen`\n\nApp 3 is a wizard wit"
    "h two stages in one bundle. **Step 1 \342\200\224 image**: a prom"
    "pt\nplus up to three uploaded references (face / outfit /"
    " pose) go to\n`POST /v1/images/edits`, or a prompt alone "
    "to `POST /v1/images/generations`.\nBoth are synchronous a"
    "nd return one `b64_json` PNG; the stage panel fills in\nt"
    "he real per-phase timings from the response's `cwick` ob"
    "ject when it arrives\n(the image endpoints have no progre"
    "ss stream, so before that it only shows\nelapsed time). T"
    "he generated PNG stays in memory and can be downloaded o"
    "r sent\nstraight to step two.\n\n**Step 2 \342\200\224 video**: the "
    "source PNG (now from step one, or uploaded directly)\nplu"
    "s a video prompt create a job with `POST /v1/videos`. Th"
    "e body carries the\nimage as an `image` data URL; the bro"
    "wser first shrinks it to a 1024px JPEG so\nthe request st"
    "ays under the server's 8 MiB body ceiling. The panel exp"
    "oses the\ncanvas (`size`), duration (`seconds`) and sampl"
    "ing budget (`steps`) \342\200\224 the last\nis an optional integer"
    " the engine clamps to 1\342\200\22330, defaulting to the full\n30-"
    "step schedule. A one-click **quick-verify preset** sets "
    "256x256 / 4 s / 4\nsteps: the smallest canvas and shortes"
    "t clip the server accepts, at a step\ncount that renders "
    "in minutes on this machine, for checking that the pipeli"
    "ne\nproduces a clean moving image before committing to a "
    "full-quality render. The app polls\n`GET /v1/videos/{id}`"
    " every two seconds \342\200\224 the progress bar follows the serv"
    "er's\nreal `progress` and `phase`, not a local timer \342\200\224 "
    "and on `completed` streams\n`GET /v1/videos/{id}/content`"
    " into a `<video>` element for inline playback and\ndownlo"
    "ad. `GET /v1/models` decides which pills read \"ready\": a"
    "n image model is\nrequired for step one, while the video "
    "model is opened on demand by the first\nPOST and therefor"
    "e shown as \"loads on first generation\" until then.\n\n**Ab"
    "out image-to-video.** The source frame really conditions"
    " the result. The\nserver decodes the uploaded image and t"
    "he visual VAE encoder maps it to a\n24-channel latent, wh"
    "ich is written into latent step 0 and held clean across\n"
    "every sampling step while the DiT attends to it. The det"
    "ail view\nreports `reference_image.conditioning = \"first_"
    "frame\"` on that path, and only\nfalls back to `\"text_only"
    "\"` if the image cannot be decoded.\n\nBoth histories (`ima"
    "ges`, `videos` keys) live in the app's own sqlite throug"
    "h\n`/v1/apps/imagegen/state`, with localStorage as the fa"
    "llback. A completed mp4\nis only retained for the lifetim"
    "e of its server job slot \342\200\224 replaying an old\nvideo row "
    "after enough later jobs have run returns 409, which the "
    "app reports\ninstead of showing a broken player.\n"
    "\000";

